        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'BODY-CENTRED CUBIC (BCC):\n\n  atoms at 8 CORNERS + 1 at the BODY CENTRE\n\n  atoms per cell = 8*(1/8) + 1 = 2\n\n  ATOMS TOUCH ALONG THE BODY DIAGONAL (not the edge!)\n\n    body diagonal length = a*sqrt(3)\n    spans 4 atomic radii: R + 2R + R\n\n    a*sqrt(3) = 4R   ->   a = 4R / sqrt(3)\n\n  COORDINATION NUMBER = 8\n\n  Examples: alpha-iron (room temp), chromium, tungsten\n\nNote: iron changes to FCC on heating - the basis of\nall steel heat treatment (Module 4).\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.3, pp.56-62 (10th ed. supplied).' },
        mistake: 'Students assume the atoms touch along the cube edge. In a body-centred cubic structure they touch along the body diagonal, and using the edge gives a lattice parameter that is wrong by a factor of root three over two.',
