        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'FACE-CENTRED CUBIC (FCC):\n\n  atoms at 8 CORNERS + 1 at each of 6 FACE CENTRES\n\n  atoms per cell = 8*(1/8) + 6*(1/2) = 1 + 3 = 4\n\n  ATOMS TOUCH ALONG THE FACE DIAGONAL\n\n    face diagonal length = a*sqrt(2)\n    spans 4 atomic radii\n\n    a*sqrt(2) = 4R   ->   a = 2R*sqrt(2)\n\n  COORDINATION NUMBER = 12  (maximum possible for\n                             equal spheres)\n  -> CLOSE PACKED\n  -> FCC metals are generally the most DUCTILE\n\n  Examples: aluminium, copper, nickel, gamma-iron (>912 C)\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.3, pp.56-62 (10th ed. supplied).' },
