        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'HEXAGONAL CLOSE-PACKED (HCP):\n\n  close packed layers stacked ABABAB...\n  (FCC stacks ABCABC... - three layer repeat)\n\n  SAME coordination number = 12\n  SAME packing efficiency as FCC\n\n  conventional cell contains 6 atoms\n  ideal c/a ratio = 1.633 (from the geometry)\n\n  Examples: magnesium, zinc, titanium, cadmium\n\nBUT: FAR LESS DUCTILE than FCC, despite identical packing\n  -> few SLIP SYSTEMS (mostly basal plane)\n  -> a polycrystal cannot accommodate arbitrary shape change\n  -> heating activates non-basal slip -> formed HOT\n\nDuctility is NOT determined by packing alone.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.3, pp.56-62 (10th ed. supplied).' },
