        definition:
          'Point defects are localised disruptions involving one or a few atomic sites. A vacancy is a missing atom, and a thermodynamically determined number of them exists in any crystal above absolute zero because they increase entropy. A self interstitial is an atom squeezed into a site between normal positions, which strains the lattice heavily and is therefore rare. Impurity atoms may substitute for host atoms on normal sites or occupy interstitial sites, and in ionic solids charge neutrality forces defects to occur in pairs, as Schottky and Frenkel defects.',
