        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'POINT DEFECTS:\n\n  VACANCY            a missing atom\n                     equilibrium number:\n                       N_v = N * exp(-Q_v / kT)\n                     -> RISES EXPONENTIALLY with T\n                     -> cannot be eliminated: ENTROPY\n                        demands them\n\n  SELF INTERSTITIAL  host atom squeezed between sites\n                     severe lattice strain -> RARE in metals\n\n  SUBSTITUTIONAL     impurity atom on a NORMAL site\n  INTERSTITIAL       impurity atom in a GAP\n                     (small atoms: C, N, H, B)\n\n  In IONIC solids, charge neutrality forces PAIRS:\n    SCHOTTKY  cation vacancy + anion vacancy\n    FRENKEL   ion moved to an interstitial site,\n              leaving its vacancy\n\nVacancies are NOT a flaw - they ENABLE DIFFUSION (Module 2).\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.4, pp.92-100 (10th ed. supplied).' },
