        definition:
          'Resolution is the smallest separation at which two features can still be distinguished as two, and it is the property that determines what an instrument can actually show. Magnification merely enlarges the image and does nothing to separate features that resolution has already merged. The resolving power of any instrument using waves is limited to roughly half the wavelength employed, so visible light cannot resolve below about two hundred nanometres. Enlarging beyond the point where resolution is exhausted produces a bigger but no more informative image, which is called empty magnification.',
