        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'GRAIN SIZE MEASUREMENT:\n\nASTM grain size number n:\n\n  N = 2^(n-1)\n\n  N = number of grains per square inch\n      at 100x magnification\n\n  LOGARITHMIC: each step of 1 in n DOUBLES the grain count\n\n  example: N = 64 = 2^6  ->  n - 1 = 6  ->  n = 7\n\nLINEAR INTERCEPT METHOD (alternative):\n  draw random test lines, count grain boundary crossings\n  mean intercept length = line length / (crossings x magnification)\n\nWHY IT IS SPECIFIED: Hall-Petch\n  sigma_y = sigma_0 + k/sqrt(d)\n  FINER grain -> HIGHER strength (and toughness)\n\nCaution: a DUPLEX structure (two grain populations)\ncannot be described by one number.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.4, pp.118-120 (10th ed. supplied).' },
