        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'DIFFUSION: net movement of atoms through a SOLID\n\n  driven by a CONCENTRATION GRADIENT\n  accomplished by atoms HOPPING between adjacent sites\n\nWHY NET FLUX GOES DOWN THE GRADIENT:\n  individual hops are RANDOM in direction\n  but there are MORE atoms on the concentrated side\n  -> more cross any plane from that side\n  -> net flux down the gradient, STATISTICALLY\n  (no atom "knows" which way the gradient points)\n\nPRACTICAL IMPORTANCE:\n  CARBURISING       harden a gear surface\n  HOMOGENISATION    remove casting segregation\n  BRAZING/SINTERING interdiffusion bonding\n  PHASE TRANSFORMATIONS that need redistribution\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.5, pp.121-126 (10th ed. supplied).' },
