        code: { lang: 'text', src: "ELASTIC CONSTANTS:\n\n  POISSON'S RATIO:\n    nu = - (lateral strain) / (axial strain)\n    typically ~0.30 for metals\n    (0.5 would mean CONSTANT VOLUME - no real solid reaches it)\n\n  SHEAR MODULUS:\n    tau = G * gamma     gamma = angular distortion\n\n  FOR AN ISOTROPIC MATERIAL these are NOT independent:\n\n    G = E / (2 * (1 + nu))\n\n  -> only TWO independent elastic constants are needed\n\n  steel: E = 207 GPa, nu = 0.30\n         G = 207 / (2 * 1.30) = 79.6 GPa   (handbook: ~80)\n\nANISOTROPIC materials (composites, single crystals)\nneed MANY more independent constants.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.152-156 (10th ed. supplied)." },
        mistake: 'Students measure the shear modulus independently for an isotropic metal. It is determined by the modulus of elasticity and Poisson ratio, so an independent value that disagrees indicates a measurement error rather than a material property.',
        book: { chapter: 6, pages: '152-156' },
        bloom: 'L4',
        co: 'CO3',
