        slides: [14, 15, 16],
        terms: ['tensile test', 'gauge length', 'elastic region', 'plastic region', 'fracture'],
        definition:
          'The tensile test pulls a standard specimen at a controlled rate while recording load and extension, from which the engineering stress-strain curve is plotted. The curve divides into a straight elastic region, a plastic region in which deformation becomes permanent and the material work hardens, a maximum at which necking begins, and a falling portion ending at fracture. Almost every mechanical property the syllabus lists is read from this one curve, which is why understanding its shape matters more than memorising the definitions separately.',
