        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'TENSILE TEST - one curve, many properties:\n\n  ELASTIC region   straight; slope = E\n  YIELD            onset of PERMANENT deformation\n  PLASTIC region   permanent; material WORK HARDENS\n                   so stress keeps RISING\n  MAXIMUM          TENSILE STRENGTH; NECKING begins here\n  FALLING portion  neck thins; engineering stress falls\n                   (because A_0 is used, not the real area)\n  FRACTURE         strain here gives DUCTILITY\n\n  AREAS under the curve:\n    to yield     = RESILIENCE\n    to fracture  = TOUGHNESS\n\nSIX+ properties from ONE specimen.\n\nBUT the test is MONOTONIC: it says NOTHING about\nrepeated loading (fatigue) or sustained loading (creep).\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.6, pp.156-160 (10th ed. supplied).' },
