        definition:
          'An isothermal transformation diagram plots the progress of austenite decomposition against time at a series of constant temperatures, producing the characteristic C shaped curves. Transformation is slow at small undercooling because the driving force is weak, and slow at large undercooling because diffusion is sluggish, so it is fastest at an intermediate temperature which forms the nose of the curve. Coarse pearlite forms just below the eutectoid, fine pearlite nearer the nose, bainite below it, and martensite forms without diffusion below the martensite start temperature.',
