        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'COMPOSITION + THERMAL HISTORY -> MICROSTRUCTURE -> PROPERTIES\n\n  COMPOSITION      fixes what phases are POSSIBLE and in\n                   what proportions AT EQUILIBRIUM\n                   -> read from the PHASE DIAGRAM\n\n  THERMAL HISTORY  fixes which possibility is REALISED,\n                   and at what SCALE\n                   -> read from the TTT / CCT DIAGRAM\n\nONE medium carbon steel, four treatments:\n\n  annealed            coarse pearlite     ~170 HB  machinable\n  normalised          fine pearlite       ~220 HB\n  water quenched      martensite          ~650 HB  UNUSABLE\n                                                   (brittle)\n  quenched + tempered tempered martensite ~400 HB  tough\n\n  a 170 to 650 HB range from ONE composition.\n\nThis is why a drawing specifies COMPOSITION **AND**\nHEAT TREATMENT. Neither alone determines the properties.\n\nIt is the Module 1 chain with its middle link explained.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.9-11, pp.251-404 (10th ed. supplied).' },
