          'A composite is a multiphase material made deliberately rather than formed naturally, combining a continuous matrix phase with a dispersed phase so that the combination has a property set neither constituent achieves alone. Composites are classified by the geometry of the dispersed phase into three groups: particle reinforced, in which the dispersed phase is roughly equiaxed, fibre reinforced, in which it has a large length to diameter ratio, and structural, in which the arrangement rather than the constituents produces the property, as in laminates and sandwich panels.',
