        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'LARGE PARTICLE COMPOSITES:\n\n  particles too LARGE for atomic-level reinforcement\n  -> mechanism is MECHANICAL: hard particles RESTRAIN\n     matrix deformation nearby and carry load\n\n  CONCRETE  gravel + sand in cement paste (the archetype)\n  CERMET    tungsten carbide in cobalt binder\n            -> carbide HARDNESS + binder TOUGHNESS\n\nMODULUS BOUNDS (rule of mixtures):\n\n  UPPER (isostrain):  E = V_p*E_p + V_m*E_m\n  LOWER (isostress):  E = 1 / (V_p/E_p + V_m/E_m)\n\n  Example: 60% particles at 350 GPa, matrix 70 GPa\n    upper = 0.6*350 + 0.4*70            = 238 GPa\n    lower = 1/(0.6/350 + 0.4/70)        = 135 GPa\n\n  the bounds are FAR APART -> they BRACKET, they do not\n  PREDICT. The real value must be measured.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.16, pp.570-578 (10th ed. supplied).' },
